# What the iltiam-staging project runs (Runbook 5, docs/runbooks/05-compose-stack.md). Public: tags only, no secrets.
# Read by scripts/deploy.sh and scripts/compose.sh as a second --env-file. One NAME=value per line; comments on their
# own lines. A tag is sha-<7> or X.Y.Z, never latest. `to-confirm` marks an image that isn't published yet:
# scripts/deploy.sh refuses to deploy it.
#
# Roll back: put the previous tags back (git log -p env/staging.versions), merge, and deploy again (Runbook 5, 9.4).

# Services beyond the always-on ones (postgres, redis, cloudflared, weights-init and the AI service), separated by
# commas. backend: migrate, web, worker and beat. web: the web app (Runbook 5, section 1). Production keeps both off
# (#36). After a deploy that turns a profile off, stop its containers by hand (Runbook 5, section 9.4).
COMPOSE_PROFILES=backend,web

# sha-a8447a3: ai-service main after #161 (per-request manual-review threshold) and #162 (registry metrics in
# /capabilities), contract-v1.1.0; linux/arm64 and linux/amd64.
AI_API_IMAGE=ghcr.io/iltiam/iltiam-ai-api:sha-a8447a3
AI_WORKER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/iltiam/iltiam-ai-worker:sha-a8447a3

# sha-8097a18: iltiam-backend main, api-v0.4.0 (#109-#119: step-up, refills, breach notices, deletion cancel, corrected
# boundary, seed_staging Super Admin) plus #121 and #122 (a value starting with $, like the Authentica key, is read as
# written). Step-up is enforced: mobile consent withdrawal and deletion get 403 STEP_UP_REQUIRED until iltiam-mobile#44.
BACKEND_IMAGE=ghcr.io/iltiam/iltiam-backend:sha-8097a18

# sha-c3552ff: iltiam-web main, Super Admin overview, clinics, doctors, audit log and AI model (read-only),
# doctor messaging and progression (#35, #38, #45, #46, #48, #49, #50).
WEB_IMAGE=ghcr.io/iltiam/iltiam-web:sha-c3552ff
